-- title:
--   Regular differentials of ℚ̄· F(Γ₁(M)) are weight-two cusp forms
-- statement:
--   Fix an integer $M \ge 1$ and a ring homomorphism $\iota_0 \colon \overline{\mathbb Q} \to \mathbb C$, where $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`. Let $F =$ [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldBar M`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L182) be the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ generated by the image, under coefficientwise extension of scalars, of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionField M`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L137) $\subseteq \mathbb Q((q))$. Let $\omega \in \Omega_{F/\overline{\mathbb Q}}$ be a Kähler differential which is regular in the sense of [`AlgebraicCurve.regularDifferentials`](def/AlgebraicCurve_RegularDifferentials.html#L26): for every place $v$ of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ — that is, every valuation subring of $F$ which contains the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, is not all of $F$, and is a principal ideal ring — there is an element $f$ of that valuation subring with $\omega = f \cdot d\pi_v$, $\pi_v$ a uniformiser of $v$. The assertion is that there exists a cusp form $f$ of weight $2$ on $\Gamma_1(M)$ such that applying $\iota_0$ to every Laurent coefficient of [`ModularCurve.diffQExp F ω`](def/ModularCurve_HeckeDifferential.html#L128) — the image of $\omega$ under the $F$-linear map on $\Omega_{F/\overline{\mathbb Q}}$ induced by the derivation $q\,d/dq$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ restricted along $F \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ — yields exactly the $q$-expansion of $f$ of width $1$, regarded as a Laurent series over $\mathbb C$.
--
--   This is the surjectivity half of the classical identification of the regular differentials on the modular curve $X_1(M)$ with the space of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_1(M)$, here in the $q$-expansion model of the function field. It is used in the construction of the linear isomorphism [`ModularCurve.exists_linearEquiv_tensor_regularDifferentials_x1FunctionFieldBar_cuspForm`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_linearEquiv_tensor_regularDifferentials_x1FunctionFieldBar_cuspForm) between (a base change of) the regular differentials and the space of cusp forms.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_cuspForm_coeffMap_diffQExp_x1FunctionFieldBar_eq_qExpansion_of_mem_regularDifferentials.lean

